  "query_preview": "..\nA monsoon band is setting up southeast of the islands. One more day\nof fairly good weather today, then it should be moving in for Sunday.\nThere's already a Hydrologic Outlook out, and a Flash Flood Watch is\na good possibility this afternoon. Wave heights will be just below \nSmall Craft Advisory criteria for Guam and Rota the next couple days,\nand just above at Tinian and Saipan. Then the sea heights will \nconverge again as they head downward.",
